==Evolution==
Evolves into '''Sweetheart Neneko''' at level 10.

Evolves into '''True Love Neneko''' at level 30 using [[Catfruit]] and XP.

==Strategy/Usage==
DO NOT get tricked by this unit's [[Wave Attack|Mini-Wave]], as the scaled down damage of said ability is hardly noticeable to any enemy except the most basic and weakest peons. Her unreliable Critical chance causes her to usually die before doing anything to stronger Metal enemies such as [[Sir Metal Seal]] or [[Super Metal Hippoe]]. Due to their high HP they will barely be phased.

When it comes to weaker Metal enemies, it is mostly a different story, as her Mini-Wave damage is enough to take out [[Metal Hippoe]], [[Metal Doge]] and even [[CyberFace]], along with a faster attack rate than other Neneko variants. With this prospect, you can treat her as a mini [[Kubiluga (Uber Rare Cat)|E. Kubilan Pasalan]], although this doesn't fix her low Critical chance, it still gives her much greater usage then a lot of other Neneko variants.

==='''True Form'''===
True Love Neneko gains a sizable 44% extra health, as well as a 20% chance to shatter [[:Category:Aku Enemies|Aku]] [[Shield]]s. Thanks to her guaranteed [[Wave Attack|Mini-Wave]] attacks that reach up to 532 range, this means that 20% of her attacks will get rid of a huge amount of the defenses on tough Aku like [[Le'Behemoth]], [[Fallen Bear]] and [[Wicked Face]].

While this sounds fantastic on paper, in practice she remains a very unreliable [[:Category:Shield Piercing Cats|Shield Piercer]] due to a few factors. Despite the increase to her base HP, True Love Neneko remains a rather frail unit relative to her lengthy cooldown, and her range is too low to outrange even Fallen Bear, which forces her to rely on using peons like [[Aku Doge]]s and [[Cerberus Kids]] as stepping stones. Even barring this, however, 20% is a rather low chance to get the Shield Pierce off when compared to far more stackable competition like [[Aku Researcher (Rare Cat)|Aku Researcher]] and [[Talents|Talented]] [[Li'l Gross Cat (Special Cat)|Li'l Macho Legs Cat]]. This is because both of them have considerably faster attacks and recharges despite their Single Attack. All of this combined leads her to be a subpar choice for a Shield Piercer, and even for those who wish to gamble for her (admittedly devastating) Area Piercing, therein lies the final problem.

True Love Neneko is a ''ridiculously'' expensive [[True Form]] to acquire, demanding three types of highly valuable [[Catfruit]]s that could very well take an average player months to obtain or just about never, until she becomes wholly obsolete. These include a Gold/Aku Catfruit that could be better spent on more versatile units like [[Lasvoss (Uber Rare Cat)|Lasvoss Reborn]], [[Gold Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Glittering Macho Cat]] or [[Mighty Deth-Troy-R (Uber Rare Cat)|Obliterator Diabolosa]]. These also include a Gold Catfruit Seed, which can currently only be obtained on [[Infernal Tower/Floor 30|Floor 30]] of the [[Infernal Tower]]. This True Form is thus barely worthwhile and should only be obtained for collection.

